WEBVTT

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:10.650
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.840
Hey there, boy.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.070
You're covered in microbes as always.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.090
Isn't that a good thing?

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.800
Only microbes would stick 
so close to me, after all.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.910
You've been visiting us frequently 
lately, haven't you?

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:40.980
I've heard all about it.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.310
Well, yeah, I guess so...

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.360
Have you hired someone new recently?

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.270
I saw a girl...

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.580
A girl?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.070
Yes, dressed all in black.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.740
A few days ago,

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.200
I saw her step out of 
the store with a broom.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.450
We didn't really talk 
or anything, but...

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.460
Are you in love, boy?

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:11.210
How nice, to be young.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.920
Sorry, but I don't know this girl.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.720
Perhaps you were mistaken?

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.650
Moyashimon

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.080
Plants secrete a unique 
substance from their roots,

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.430
The Gothic Lolita's Kiss

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.800
which attracts countless 
microorganisms.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.350
The roots also utilize 
the organic matter

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:54.020
produced by these microorganisms.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:56.690
Now, take a look at this slide.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.470
<i>Why...</i>

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.030
<i>...does that girl in 
black get to me so much?</i>

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:07.050
Hey...

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.040
Yeah?

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:11.710
Yuuki-kun hasn't been coming 
to class lately, has he?

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.540
I don't see him around campus, either.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.540
What's he up to?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.780
I've been wondering the same thing.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.550
Oh, yeah! Are you free after this?

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.500
Yeah, I guess.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.350
Will you come shopping with me?

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.370
Sure.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.330
Okay, thanks.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.330
Maybe I should go find out...

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:41.840
Not here?

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.320
Just a quick peek...

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.340
Hello.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.090
H-H-H—

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.600
Sawaki Souemon Tadayasu.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.430
Y-Yeah...

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.750
Did Mr. Hiyoshi tell you about me?

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.980
No. I've always known.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.980
You've... always known me?

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:19.990
Uh huh.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.870
Were your eyes always that big?

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.630
Oh, this is just makeup.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.630
Why did Sawaki-kun go home?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.400
I asked him to come shopping with me.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.630
Wonder if I can catch up.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.780
If I do, I'll make him buy me dinner...

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.970
You don't seem very surprised.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:02.280
No, my brain's just too panicked 
to understand what's going on.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:04.780
A gothic lolita girl...

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:26.210
You didn't notice the 
first time you saw me?

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:27.190
N-No.

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:28.170
Really?

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.470
I thought my microbes 
would give me away.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:34.730
I-I don't think I'm that 
good at recognizing them!

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.360
Besides, if I'd guessed by your 
microbes and got it wrong,

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:40.230
I'd have been taken for a weirdo.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.690
Well, a lot has changed for me, too.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.240
Y-You saw?

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.660
Wh-Which part exactly?

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.440
Oh! I promised I'd go 
somewhere with you!

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.530
Th-That's right!

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.170
I asked you to come shopping with me!

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.670
It's okay. I can handle it by myself.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.390
That won't do.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:06.670
You need to keep your promises.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.610
Off you go. See you later, Sawaki...

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:16.820
-kun.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.490
What were you doing,

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.500
right there in the 
street in the daytime?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.410
I'm not really sure myself...

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.690
So what are you buying?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.290
It's going to get hot soon,

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.200
so I want a mat for my room.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:34.500
And wipe your mouth off before 
you try to change the subject.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.700
It looks so wrong, all black like that.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:42.670
Disinfected

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.180
This is heavy...

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:46.770
You could've just had it delivered.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:49.220
When I buy something, 
I want to use it right away.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:52.030
We have to take this onto the train?

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.600
Of course.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.220
I came by train, so I have 
to go home by train.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:59.610
Can we stop somewhere 
for a drink, Oikawa?

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.350
I've got barley tea at home. 
Just hang in there.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.680
You want me to help 
you lay it down, too?

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:06.410
Obviously!

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.740
I've got curry, so you can 
have dinner before you leave.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:14.550
Oikawa, just grab a strap.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.260
No way! They're covered with germs!

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:19.130
Then try harder to stand still!

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.330
Complain to the driver, not me!

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:32.210
Sorry, can you wait here 
for about five minutes?

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.900
I'm going to tidy up a bit.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:39.470
Oh, yeah... this will be my 
first time in a girl's room.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.000
Okay, I'm done!

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.040
Huh?

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.450
Is that what you call five minutes?

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:06.740
I'm roasting out here!

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:08.500
Really? Sorry about that...

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:15.630
You made me wait while you 
took a shower, didn't you?

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:17.760
Yeah... it just sort of happened.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.560
Well, come in. The AC's on.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.520
Germ-Free 
Life

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.520
Refresh

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.520
Clean Sheets

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.520
Air 
Freshener

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.520
Antibacterial 
with Alcohol

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.520
Clean & 
Odorless

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.520
<i>Wh-What's with this room?</i>

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.820
<i>There are no microbes. 
It's totally sterile.</i>

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.030
Hey, don't look around at everything!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:34.250
We can't sit down until the 
mat is down, so hurry up.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:39.620
This mat slides around a lot.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:40.660
Yeah.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.320
It could be dangerous.

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.410
Maybe we should put some 
tape on the bottom.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.170
The tape's in the closet.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:49.050
Okay, I'll get it.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.460
No!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.460
You wait in the bathroom, Sawaki-kun.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:53.170
Huh?

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:57.910
The closet of a woman living 
alone houses a whole universe.

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.440
If you open it, you'll get hurt.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:01.680
You'll get burned. You'll regret it!

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.180
Go on. I'll call you 
when I've closed it.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.920
What's with her?

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:15.590
I don't get women. Or at least Oikawa.

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:22.450
Okay, let's eat!

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:24.550
Wow, this looks great!

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.840
So you cook for yourself?

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.560
Of course I do.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:31.460
Living alone in Tokyo is 
a battle with budgets.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.390
Mm, it's good.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:42.040
Hey, Sawaki-kun...

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.100
Is there something about you?

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.190
S-Something?

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:50.610
You know, like at orientation...

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.860
Everyone! Don't eat this!

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.280
Don't eat this!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.240
There's something really bad in it!

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.240
Every now and then, 
you've made me wonder.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:02.220
You do say weird stuff 
sometimes, you know?

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.600
D-Do I?

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:07.510
But nobody else seems bothered by it.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:13.850
I was starting to think I'm the only 
one in the dark about something.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.010
But I guess it's okay.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:23.260
I was the only one who got to 
see a secret of yours today.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.840
Are you dating that girl?

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:30.500
Come on, tell your big sister.

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:33.150
No, it's not like that.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.440
Barley 
Tea

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.030
I'll cheer you on.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.140
As your friend, you can 
ask me anything, okay?

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:40.520
But I like older guys, 
so I probably don't think

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.030
on the same level as you.

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:45.230
Go for it, Sawaki-kun!

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.290
Uh... thanks?

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:50.640
Thanks for your help. 
Careful going home.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:52.960
I will. Thanks for dinner.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:58.260
<i>She likes older guys?</i>

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:02.740
<i>Still, I don't know if I should tell</i>

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:06.790
<i>Oikawa and the others 
about Kei or not...</i>

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.180
Did something good happen today?

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.330
Y-Yeah...

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:30.450
Could you store these in 
the refrigerator for me?

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:31.330
Sure.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:38.340
How nice indeed, to be young...

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.870
Yah!

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.870
Smooch

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:44.870
Hey, people are watching!

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:46.850
Everyone Assemble<i>!</i>

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:51.510
What do you think?

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.540
How long have these been here?

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:57.980
I'm sure they're fine. I'm starving.

00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.550
What's up?

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.210
It's this bread.

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:03.670
There are no microbes on it.

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:04.720
Oh, good!

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:07.470
I feel a lot better knowing 
this gets the OK from you!

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:08.620
Hey, Sawaki!

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:11.620
Would you start helping me 
identify microbes already?

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:14.190
My doctoral thesis is really difficult.

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:15.500
Help me out.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.400
But I don't know if I 
could be much help.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:22.380
The microbes I see look nothing 
like the ones in your photos.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.560
But you've been learning, haven't you?

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:28.140
Don't you know enough to start 
putting together reports by now?

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:31.480
By now? It's only my first year.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.030
You never know.

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:36.650
Maybe that ability will disappear 
when you lose your virginity.

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.970
P-Please cut that out.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.080
I'm pretty sure that won't happen.

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.520
You don't have classes this afternoon?

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.190
Oh... I was thinking 
of heading home now.

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:48.720
I have some things to do. Later.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:55.870
Things to do, eh?

00:12:56.490 --> 00:13:00.200
Well, I guess it'll take some 
time before I can use Sawaki.

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:03.040
It'll be pointless if he 
doesn't learn more first.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.680
Maybe I'm the only one 
who's in a hurry.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:08.150
This... tastes kinda sour.

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:10.340
Yeah, it's not doing 
much for my appetite.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.620
Those are spoiled.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.690
Should I call Kei?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.610
He probably won't answer anyway.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:29.700
And if he does, what would I say?

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:37.430
Ow, hot!

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:43.800
That's rare... it's totally quiet.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.220
Why...

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.280
That bread is the only 
reason I can think of.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:53.970
Yeah, but Sawaki said there 
weren't any microbes on it.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:56.070
Don't be stupid!

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:58.090
There's no point in blaming Sawaki.

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:00.980
His ability to see microbes 
is just like a bonus.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.840
I'm not blaming him!

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:04.900
But... maybe there are 
occasionally times

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.490
when he can't see them?

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.990
Don't ask me. 
Only Sawaki would know that.

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.240
Kawahama!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.050
Let me use the western toilet now!

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:17.620
They're being so quiet...

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:23.130
I guess it's only normal to think 
he can't see them anymore.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.830
Maybe...

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:30.260
Octopus! Squid

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:30.260
Don't draw here!! 
Same to you

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.320
It'd be faster to ask Sawaki.

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.260
Yeah, but is it really that simple?

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:34.260
Stupid

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:32.470
Wouldn't he be shocked to learn that

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.260
he suddenly can't see them anymore?

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:37.390
And I guess we have to 
consider what happens

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:39.520
if Hasegawa and Itsuki find out.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:43.250
If you look at it from 
Sawaki's perspective,

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:45.850
I think all the relationships 
he has with people here

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:48.530
can be credited to his ability.

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:49.780
Probably.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:52.320
So if he can't see microbes anymore,

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.290
wouldn't it ruin those relationships?

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.790
So, he would keep it a secret?

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:02.290
We should at least wait for 
him to tell us himself.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:09.400
It's not like we know for 
sure that he can't see them.

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:12.550
All we need to do is look 
out for our underclassman.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.030
Don't try to sound cool 
when you've got the runs!

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:17.310
Switch toilets with me again!

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:19.970
Are you stupid? We just switched!

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:22.110
Shut up! Do you realize 
how much strength

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:24.690
it takes for a fat guy to squat?!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.440
Misato                                 Kawahama

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:35.700
Professor...

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:39.200
Chrysogenum... so it's blue mold.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.770
I see, I see.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.210
There are no microbes on it.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:50.720
That fool.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.800
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:10.780
Oh, thank you.

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:20.700
<i>Who is this girl, anyway?</i>

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:24.710
Sawaki gets mad when 
you call him a "shrimp."

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:27.780
Really? I wonder if I've 
ever called him that...

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:31.760
We got into a fight over that 
once, when we were little.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:34.760
No way! Sawaki-kun gets into fights?

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.490
We were in grade school.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:39.450
I guess he still doesn't like 
talking about the past.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:40.700
Hmm...

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:46.520
<i>Maybe she and Sawaki-kun 
were childhood friends?</i>

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:50.950
You know...

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:55.050
We've only been talking about 
Sawaki-kun, haven't we?

00:16:58.020 --> 00:16:59.850
I have to ask...

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:02.540
Do you like him?

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:06.540
I can't say. It wouldn't be right.

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.880
Why? There's nothing wrong with it!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.550
That's good, isn't it?

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:11.780
You do like him, right?

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:13.060
What do you like about him?

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:15.050
Come on, tell your big sister!

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:17.940
That he's short.

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.560
You're right. You can't tell him that.

00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:24.660
It's weird, isn't it? 
Don't tell him, okay?

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:26.560
No, it's not weird at all!

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:29.940
It's not?

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:33.270
In fact, I'll cheer you on.

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:35.980
Oh...

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:39.060
I'm kind of glad I told you.

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:44.950
But Sawaki likes girls 
like you, Oikawa-san.

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:48.860
No, no way!

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:50.570
There's no way he likes me!

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:51.840
Really?

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.850
And how do you feel?

00:17:53.850 --> 00:17:56.390
I like older guys.

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:58.560
I hang out with Sawaki-kun a lot,

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:00.820
but I've never even thought 
about him that way.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:01.820
Really?

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:02.960
Yes, really!

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.720
But when I first saw you,

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:08.730
I thought Sawaki would like you.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:12.320
But I guess he got a 
bad first impression.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.730
You did come in wearing nose 
plugs and carrying a stingray.

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:18.450
<i>How does she know about that?</i>

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.740
Did Sawaki-kun tell you that?

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:21.650
Huh?

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:27.250
Oops... you mean Sawaki 
didn't tell you?

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:28.530
Huh?

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:32.210
Sawaki...

00:18:32.660 --> 00:18:34.300
Want to work part-time with us?

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:37.720
Itsuki hasn't asked you for 
much help lately, right?

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.600
Work part-time?

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:42.000
Well, I guess I don't have much money.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.090
Work with us, huh? Nice one.

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:46.320
Nah, it's just a temporary escape.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:50.230
I just want to get Sawaki away 
from the lab for a while.

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:53.130
If Sawaki can't see microbes anymore,

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:56.400
we don't know what they'll 
say, especially Hasegawa.

00:18:58.710 --> 00:19:00.770
Anyway, we'll check 
the bulletin board and

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:03.320
find out if the head office 
has any part-time openings.

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:04.410
Yeah.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:14.920
You think she...

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:17.420
Sawaki, come here.

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:29.730
Come over here, Sawaki.

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.530
Remember these?

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.420
The bread we ate yesterday.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:38.940
Yeah... I remember now.

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:42.460
Sawaki...

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:46.450
You can't see any microbes, can you?

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.960
You can't, can you?

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.340
Moyashimon

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.340
Episode 10

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.340
Microbe Theater

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.340
Microbe Theater 10!

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:29.350
Kawahama

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:33.850
What's wrong?

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:35.820
You seem down.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:38.100
Is it too cold for you to brew?

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:40.020
It's Tadayasu...

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.690
Tadayasu?

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:44.030
What about Tadayasu?

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:48.030
It looks like he can't see us anymore.

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:49.560
So what?

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:51.120
What's so bad about that?

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:53.040
There's nothing wrong with that.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:56.040
Microbes only care about 
propagating, after all!

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.490
What are you saying?

00:21:57.490 --> 00:21:59.480
If Tadayasu can't see us anymore,

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:02.040
that means we'll all return 
to our original forms!

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:02.800
What?

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:05.800
I don't want to be seen this way!

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:08.800
The image I've had all 
this time is ruined!

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.800
Don't look if you don't 
want to! It's too creepy!

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:15.160
As you can see, this is 
what we really look like.

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:18.700
But Tadayasu captures our features 
pretty well, doesn't he?

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:21.810
By the way, I look like this.

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:24.820
Tadayasu, you jerk!

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:29.820
In Microbe Theater 
Episode 11,

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:29.820
We'll Do the Brewing.

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:36.250
Next Week: 
"A Shining Microbe Future"

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:34.350
Agonize and worry, young people!
